  <h3 class="linklist">Bolex Reporter, Volume 17</h3>
  <!-- EPHEMERA and bolex reporter stuff -->
  <div id="books"> 
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltright" src="../images/reporter/17_1.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="283"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">1967</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 17, Number 1</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "Verifying a Discovery", Geza 
        de Rosner; "From Mountain to Desert", Major Mike Banks; "A New Way of 
        Seeing", Peter Vanadia; "Alpine Flight", Robert A. Mickelsen; "Filming 
        Summer Indians", William Holloway; "Focus in on Nature", Daniel Lyons, 
        Peter Fetko and Leonard Rue; "The Neglected Art - Editing", William A. 
        Keith; "Unusual Ski Films", Hans Gmoser; "A Happy Choice of Camera", Mel 
        Baldwin; "Filming in Vietnam", Tony Munday</li>
      <li class="desc">The first Bolex super 8mm camera is reviewed in this issue, 
        along with the newest line of super 8 projectors: the SM8 and 18-5 Super. 
        The new H-16 REX-5, with 400 foot magazine and accessories, is also introduced. 
      </li>
      <li class="pp">32 pages</li>
    </ul>
    <hr>
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/reporter/17_2.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="283"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">1967-1968</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 17, Number 2</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "A Day at the Races", E. Abraben; 
        "An Idea is Born", Carlton Schammel; "The Lens That Does the Impossible", 
        William A. Keith; "Alaskan Adventure", Wolfgang Bayer; "A Trip to the 
        South Pole", John P. Elden; "Nature Walkabout", Vincent Serventy; "A New 
        Amphibian for Maryland", Daniel J. Lyons; "The Sahara is a Woman", Bill 
        Hill; "A Science Documentary at Sea", Willard Bascom; "Educational Television", 
        Rev. Brother Charles Felix, FSC</li>
      <li class="desc">The SM8 projector and 150 camera are reviewed again; although 
        both read more like a brochure or advertisement.</li>
      <li class="pp">32 pages</li>
    </ul>
